    {
      "name": "Oldenborn",
      "type": "species",
      "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC_Character_Options/Oldenborne_Earthbound_2.png",
      "system": {
        "category": "ancestry",
        "source": {
          "custom": "Bad Eden",
          "rules": "2024",
          "revision": 2,
          "book": "",
          "license": ""
        },
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Oldenborn.</strong> Normalized Bad Eden ancestry root.</p><p>Select one heritage separately when building the character: <strong>Earthbound, Lumenwrought, Stormborn Nomad, Rustland Scavenger</strong>.</p><p>This root grants the shared Oldenborn core trait package and preserves live UUID compatibility for existing feature items.</p><p><em>\u201cYou are not an elf. You are the memory of a place that learned to walk again.\u201d</em></p>\n<p><strong>Dream-Flesh.</strong> You do not sleep. When you rest, you drift into Yesod\u2014symbolic memory-space\u2014unless you choose otherwise. You are immune to magical sleep, and you can always tell when a dream, illusion, or constructed reality is present.</p>\n<p><strong>Old Memory, Old Paths.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on checks to interpret ruins, follow ley-lines, identify altered terrain, and sense metaphysical instability. You always know if a place feels <em>remembered</em>, <em>abandoned</em>, or <em>contested</em> (the GM answers vaguely).</p>\n<p><strong>Veil-Sight.</strong> You perceive the <em>presence</em> of spirits, ghosts, Spark echoes, and noospheric constructs. This grants awareness, not perfect sight.</p>\n<p><strong>You Are Remembered.</strong> When you first meet a community, the GM chooses (or rolls) whether you are met with reverence, fear, or familiarity. It\u2019s never neutral.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
